  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p31.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let each equal side be \\(a\\) and half the base be \\(b.\\) The perimeter gives \\(a+b=16.\\) The altitude bisects the base, so \\[ a^2-b^2=8^2. \\] Thus \\((a-b)(a+b)=64,\\) giving \\(a-b=4.\\) Hence \\(b=6,\\) so the base is \\(12.\\) The area is \\[ \\frac12(12)(8)=48. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Let each equal side be \\(a\\) and half the base be \\(b\\)",
        "Use \\(a+b=16\\) and \\(a^2-b^2=8^2\\)"
      ],
